<BlogLayout
  title="Scan-to-BIM: How a Point Cloud Becomes a Revit Model"
  description="A plain-language walkthrough of the scan-to-BIM workflow, capture, registration, modeling to a target LOD, and QA, and where projects go wrong when the steps get rushed."
  category="Guide"
  readTime="8 min"
>
  <p>"Scan-to-BIM" gets said like it's one thing. It isn't. It's a chain of four distinct steps, and the quality of the final Revit model depends on every one of them being done properly. When a model comes back wrong, it's almost always because a step got skipped or rushed. Here's the whole chain, in order, in plain language.</p>

